@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title PLANNED — a self-defending pipeline (no CI exists yet)

actor "push / PR" as PUSH

node "CI runner — standard" as STD <<host>> {
  component "static analysis\ngofmt -l · go vet · golangci-lint · go build" as SA <<app>>
  component "L1 unit + L2 contract\ngo test -race ./... (no Docker)" as L12 <<app>>
}

node "CI runner — Docker" as DKR <<host>> {
  component "L3 egress infra-integration\nPROVEO_EGRESS_INTEGRATION=1\n-tags=integration" as L3 <<async>>
  component "image graph build\nbase → base-node → base-node-lsp →\nbase-node-browser → harnesses + sidecars" as IMG <<async>>
}

node "CI runner — GPU (or pinned small model)" as GPU <<host>> {
  component "L4 agent E2E\nPROVEO_LLM_TEST=1 -tags=e2e" as L4 <<async>>
}

PUSH ARROW_MAIN SA
SA ARROW_MAIN L12
L12 ARROW_QUEUE L3
L12 ARROW_QUEUE IMG
L3 ARROW_QUEUE L4
IMG ARROW_QUEUE L4

note right of SA
  **Already enforced locally, not in CI.** ""mise run ci""
  runs exactly these gates and is green; ""\.golangci.yml""
  exists. What is missing is a ""\.github/workflows"" that
  runs it on every push — today nothing stops a regression
  from landing.
end note

note right of L4
  Both suites exist and pass: ""e2e_test.go"" (local model,
  opencode) and ""hello_world_test.go"" (cloud model, all
  three harnesses, firewall + broker). CI needs a GPU
  runner for the former, or a pinned small model via
  ""PROVEO_TEST_LOCAL_MODEL"" on CPU.
  Detail: _spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml
end note

note bottom of IMG
  ""\.goreleaser.yaml"" covers the **binary** only. Nothing
  builds the image graph on push, so a Dockerfile break is
  found by a human running ""mise run build"".
end note

note bottom of DKR
  **Then — supply chain, once the pipeline exists:**
  * digest-pin the enforcement images (""ubuntu/squid"",
    ""proveo/egress-proxy"", ""ollama/ollama"") — the egress
    trust root, currently floating ""latest""
  * make the advertised CDN install self-verifying, or
    sign the artifacts (today checksum + binary share an
    origin)
  * full egress validation matrix: per-mode invariants +
    active Squid / proxy readiness probes
  * pre-bake ""@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"" so opencode's
    local model resolves under firewall (runtime install
    is blocked by the locked egress)
end note
@enduml
